{"name":"Royal Palm","hex":"#418d84","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"royal palm","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the genus Roystonea of palm trees, native to the Caribbean Islands and the adjacent coasts of Florida and Central and South America, but grown throughout the tropics and subtropics for its great height and elegant form\nespecially of the species Roystonea regia.","especially of the species Roystonea regia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/royal_palm"}],"entries":[{"title":"Roystonea regia","blocks":[{"text":"Roystonea regia, commonly known as the royal palm, Cuban royal palm, or Florida royal palm, is a species of palm native to Mexico, the Caribbean, Florida, and parts of Central America. A large and attractive palm, it has been planted throughout the tropics and subtropics as an ornamental tree. Although it is sometimes called R. elata, the conserved name R. regia is now the correct name for the species. The royal palm reaches heights from 15–24 m (50–80 ft) tall. Populations in Cuba and Florida were long seen as separate species, but are now considered a single species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Roystonea_regia.jpg/330px-Roystonea_regia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roystonea_regia","wikidata":"Q1069046"},{"title":"Royal Palm (train)","blocks":[{"text":"The Royal Palm was a named train of the Southern Railway that ran from Cincinnati, Ohio, to Jacksonville, Florida, and then on the Florida East Coast Railway's East Coast Champion to Miami, Florida. The train was discontinued in 1970."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Royal_Palm_Southern_Railway.JPG/330px-Royal_Palm_Southern_Railway.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Palm_(train)","wikidata":"Q7374673"}],"i